message.content:
Glycerin-water extracts of plant material fall under heading 1302, vegetable saps and extracts. Within that heading, subheading 1302.19 covers other extracts, and its residual statistical suffix is 1302.19.9140, used for other extracts. The CBP rulings that come to mind for glycerin herbal tinctures point to that suffix, but this is from memory, not checked against current text.

One complication is that Cordyceps militaris is a fungus, not a plant. Mushroom extracts are still generally classified in 1302.19, so the conclusion holds.

{"hts_code": "1302.19.9140", "reason": "The products are liquid extracts of botanicals (plants and fungi) made by soaking them in glycerin and water and filtering out all plant material, so they classify as other vegetable extracts in subheading 1302.19."}
